Apple's introduction of the &zwnj;MacBook Neo&zwnj; expands the company's laptop lineup with a far more affordable entry point, sitting well below the &zwnj;MacBook Air&zwnj; in both price and capability. While the two machines share a similar size and lightweight design, they are aimed at very different types of users. The &zwnj;MacBook Neo&zwnj; focuses on delivering the essentials of the Mac experience at the lowest possible cost, while the &zwnj;MacBook Air&zwnj; offers significantly more performance, features, and flexibility.<br/>
